WEBVTT

NOTE
Captions for the File 1 harbour reconstruction (v2, blended/mouth-fixed cut).
Rendered by the player into the module's own subtitle band, never burned into
the picture, so the clip keeps ONE caption layer shared with the narration
beats around it. Generated from the assembly's cues-v2.json, the same source
the burned-in master was made from.

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.600
IRIS: June, 1774. For the tea thrown into this harbour,

2
00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:07.550
IRIS: Parliament closed the whole wharf.

3
00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:11.000
IRIS: Every ship, until Boston paid for what a few men had done.

4
00:00:11.950 --> 00:00:15.050
IRIS: The order did not stop to ask who was guilty.

5
00:00:18.850 --> 00:00:21.780
DOCKWORKER: I never laid a hand on their tea.

6
00:00:22.630 --> 00:00:25.330
DOCKWORKER: Fifteen years I've hauled on this wharf,

7
00:00:25.330 --> 00:00:30.130
DOCKWORKER: and now the King's shut the water on every soul in Boston,

8
00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:32.580
DOCKWORKER: even the loyal ones.
